  8	---
  9	
 10	**What this demands of an implementation:** The canonical factory deployment may deliberately rely on one quote token and one Chainlink wrapper, but those identities must be fixed outside sponsor and buyer control. Per-raffle callers must not be able to substitute another payment token or randomness wrapper. Conversely, a sponsor-selected prize contract and a buyer-selected ticket recipient must be handled as adversarial external code: their callbacks and return values cannot be promoted into security-critical facts merely because they claim an interface or return an expected value.
 11	
 12	---
 13	
 14	**Where enforcement lives:**
 15	
 16	The trusted dependency identities are constructor inputs stored in immutable factory fields. Construction checks that both addresses contain code, checks only six-decimal metadata for the quote token, fixes both addresses, and deploys the sole raffle implementation with those same values:
 17	
 18	```solidity
 19	// target/packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:L65-L78
 20	constructor(address quoteToken_, address vrfWrapper_, address protocolTreasury_) {
 21	    _requireContract(quoteToken_);
 22	    _requireContract(vrfWrapper_);
 23	    if (protocolTreasury_ == address(0)) revert ZeroAddress();
 24	
 25	    uint8 quoteDecimals = 0;
 26	    try IERC20Metadata(quoteToken_).decimals() returns (uint8 decimals_) {
 27	        quoteDecimals = decimals_;
 28	    } catch {
 29	        revert UnsupportedQuoteToken(quoteToken_);
 30	    }
 31	    if (quoteDecimals != RaffleConstants.QUOTE_TOKEN_DECIMALS) {
 32	        revert InvalidQuoteTokenDecimals(quoteDecimals, RaffleConstants.QUOTE_TOKEN_DECIMALS);
 33	    }
 34	```
 35	
 36	```solidity
 37	// target/packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:L85-L91
 38	quoteToken = quoteToken_;
 39	vrfWrapper = vrfWrapper_;
 40	protocolTreasury = protocolTreasury_;
 41	
 42	address implementation = address(new Raffle(quoteToken_, vrfWrapper_));
 43	if (protocolTreasury_ == implementation) revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(protocolTreasury_);
