 46	
 47	The factory explicitly assigns proof of official-USDC identity to deployment tooling rather than trying to infer identity from token metadata (`target/packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:L58-L63`; `target/packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:L6-L9`). Thus the source establishes a deployment trust anchor, not the actual mainnet identity of the supplied address.
 48	
 49	Per-raffle sponsors have no quote-token or wrapper field to supply. Their creation struct contains only the sponsor recipient, prize token and ID, reserve, and end time (`target/packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:L14-L26`). `createRaffle` clones the immutable `raffleImplementation` and passes only clone-local fields, including the sponsor-selected prize token, to `initialize`:
 50	
 51	```solidity
 52	// target/packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:L105-L121
 53	uint256 raffleId = ++raffleCount;
 54	raffle = Clones.clone(raffleImplementation);
 55	// The fresh fixed-target clone can initialize only once; this function is nonReentrant and atomic.
 56	// slither-disable-next-line reentrancy-no-eth
 57	IRaffle(raffle)
 58	    .initialize(
 59	        IRaffle.RaffleInitParams({
 60	        sponsor: msg.sender,
 61	        sponsorRecipient: params.sponsorRecipient,
 62	        protocolTreasury: protocolTreasury,
 63	        prizeToken: params.prizeToken,
 64	        prizeTokenId: params.prizeTokenId,
 65	        raffleId: raffleId,
 66	        reserveEntries: params.reserveEntries,
 67	        endTime: params.endTime
 68	    })
 69	    );
