 71	
 72	`Clones.clone` embeds the supplied implementation in the proxy bytecode and delegates to that fixed address (`target/packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/Clones.sol:L47-L62`). The implementation stores `factory` and `quoteToken` as immutables (`target/packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:L52-L59`); its constructor fixes the quote token and passes the wrapper to an inherited immutable (`target/packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:L151-L166`; `target/packages/contracts/node_modules/@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/VRFV2PlusWrapperConsumerBase.sol:L34-L47`). Clone initialization is one-time, factory-only, and has no branch that writes either dependency (`target/packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:L176-L205`).
 73	
 74	Every quote-token movement uses that immutable field: purchases call it at `target/packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:L223-L225`, and every payout funnels through `_transferQuote` at `target/packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:L560-L567`. `SafeERC20` validates call success or an optional boolean return but does not verify balance deltas (`target/packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol:L176-L200`, `L212-L244`), so exact fee-free, non-rebasing movement is deliberately on the trusted side of the boundary. Wrapper pricing and requests likewise use the inherited immutable (`target/packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:L249-L260`, `L435-L448`), and `rawFulfillRandomWords` rejects every caller other than that immutable wrapper before dispatch (`target/packages/contracts/node_modules/@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/VRFV2PlusWrapperConsumerBase.sol:L101-L107`).
 75	
 76	Ticket recipients are caller-selected at `buyEntries`, but the purchase is guarded while the ticket is safely minted:
