108	
109	The inherited `_safeMint` writes ownership and then invokes the contract recipient (`target/packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:L279-L290`); the receiver utility requires the exact acceptance selector and reverts or bubbles failure (`target/packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/utils/ERC721Utils.sol:L25-L48`). The active `nonReentrant` modifier brackets that callback (`target/packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:L69-L73`, `L94-L105`). Mint and transfer updates additionally reject the factory, implementation, quote token, wrapper, prize token, this raffle, and registered sibling raffles as ticket destinations (`target/packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:L491-L502`, `L587-L605`). These paths do not give an arbitrary recipient a dependency role.
110	
111	The gap is the sponsor-selected prize contract. Although its address is excluded from the quote-token and wrapper identities (`target/packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol:L154-L169`), acceptance relies on claims made by that same address. It supplies the ERC-165 answer:
