151	The receiver checks the callback tuple before entering `Active` (`target/packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:L409-L431`), but a sponsor-selected contract controls whether it calls that receiver and what its own `ownerOf` returns. Later prize delivery again accepts the selected contract's `transferFrom` execution and `ownerOf` report (`target/packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:L327-L337`, `L395-L406`). The production interface makes this trust explicit: “Supported prizes are honest, standards-compliant ERC-721s” (`target/packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:L12-L15`). Consequently, the prize path does not implement the specification's untrusted-contract side: a contract that returns the expected interface and ownership answers can reach publication without an independently established ERC-721 ledger or transferable prize. It cannot replace the immutable quote token, but it is granted an honesty assumption over the security-critical fact of prize escrow and delivery.
