180	
181	**How the verdict was reached:** This is `partial`, not `implemented`, because the fixed quote-token/wrapper and ticket-recipient paths enforce the declared sides of the boundary, but the prize path requires an attacker-selected contract to be honest and treats its interface, callback, transfer, and ownership reports as the facts that activate and publish a raffle. It is not `contradicted` as a whole because no sponsor or buyer can replace the stored quote token or wrapper, all quote flows use the stored token, wrapper callbacks are sender-authenticated, and ticket-recipient callbacks are explicitly handled as external interactions. It is not `absent`: the immutables, factory-only initialization, fixed clone target, destination screening, safe-receiver check, and reentrancy guard are concrete enforcement. The precise missing portion is adversarial treatment of the arbitrary prize contract on the successful self-report branch.
